From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:28:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mach: Add a --js-engine option to build on QuickJS

`./mach build --js-engine quickjs`, or `js-engine = "quickjs"` in
.servobuild, builds Servo on servo-quickjs, the QuickJS implementation
of the mozjs API. mach passes support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml, which
patches mozjs to the servo-quickjs commit it pins, to every cargo
command of a build configuration, also with `-p`, and enables the
js-quickjs feature where it passes features. Before, a QuickJS build
needed a hand-written patch in .cargo/config.toml, and the pinned commit
lived in quickjs.yml, from where the runner image and the servo-ohos-wpt
nightly had to extract it.

The patch replaces mozjs in Cargo.lock, so a QuickJS build can't be
`--locked`, and a cargo command without the configuration, e.g. from
rust-analyzer, switches Cargo.lock back to SpiderMonkey. SpiderMonkey
builds are unchanged. quickjs.yml builds with the option, and its
servo-quickjs-ref input now replaces the commit in the file. A change
under support/quickjs/ runs only the QuickJS build.

Fork note: the pinned commit is bumped with mozjs at each sync, as it
was in quickjs.yml.

Validation: `./mach build --release --js-engine quickjs` built servoshell on servo-quickjs 72fa2b6 (cargo's command had the configuration and js-quickjs; the binary has the QuickJS symbols and no SpiderMonkey ones) and `xvfb-run ./mach smoketest --release` passed. With a nonexistent extra `--config`, mach printed the expected cargo commands for `--js-engine quickjs`, for js-engine = "quickjs" in .servobuild, for no option (unchanged) and for `--js-engine spidermonkey` overriding .servobuild; an unknown value in .servobuild is an error. `./mach check --js-engine quickjs -p servo-url` left the QuickJS Cargo.lock. `./mach test-scripts` and `./mach test-tidy` pass; actionlint reports for quickjs.yml only its two findings on ohos-main.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, which also ran the builds and checks above)
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; 2026-10-22 sync -- upstream #48934 no longer adds `media-gstreamer` in mach (it is a default feature now; dummy-media builds switch to `--no-default-features` + `default_base`): the `js-quickjs` feature is appended after that block)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 .github/workflows/quickjs.yml     | 15 +++++++--------
 python/servo/command_base.py      | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 python/servo/pr_jobs.py           |  4 ++--
 servobuild.example                |  5 +++++
 support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml |  8 ++++++++
 5 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml

diff --git a/.github/workflows/quickjs.yml b/.github/workflows/quickjs.yml
index ee77453600e..2a29c84798e 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/quickjs.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/quickjs.yml
@@ -44,9 +44,8 @@ env:
   RUST_BACKTRACE: 1
   SHELL: /bin/bash
   SERVO_QUICKJS_URL: https://github.com/openharmony-rs/servo-quickjs
-  # The servo-quickjs commit this tree builds with. Bump it with mozjs at each sync, so that older
-  # commits keep building with the shim they were tested with.
-  SERVO_QUICKJS_REF: ${{ inputs.servo-quickjs-ref || '72fa2b6697a60889969397313ad23405196c5b4e' }}
+  # Replaces the servo-quickjs commit pinned in support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml, if set.
+  SERVO_QUICKJS_REF: ${{ inputs.servo-quickjs-ref }}
   PROFILE: ${{ inputs.profile || 'release' }}
   RUN_WPT: ${{ github.event_name == 'schedule' || inputs.wpt }}
 
@@ -101,9 +100,8 @@ jobs:
             echo "RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache"
             echo "CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0"
           } >> "$GITHUB_ENV"
-      # `mach` cannot pass `--config`, so the patch goes into `.cargo/config.toml`. It changes
-      # Cargo.lock, so the build below is not `--locked`.
-      - name: Patch mozjs to the QuickJS shim
+      - name: Use another servo-quickjs commit
+        if: ${{ env.SERVO_QUICKJS_REF != '' }}
         run: |
           refs=$(git ls-remote "$SERVO_QUICKJS_URL")
           rev=
@@ -116,10 +114,11 @@ jobs:
             echo "::error::$SERVO_QUICKJS_REF is not a branch or tag of $SERVO_QUICKJS_URL, nor a full commit hash"
             exit 1
           fi
-          printf '\n[patch.crates-io]\nmozjs = { git = "%s", rev = "%s" }\n' "$SERVO_QUICKJS_URL" "$rev" >> .cargo/config.toml
+          sed -i -E "s/rev = \"[0-9a-f]{40}\"/rev = \"$rev\"/" support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml
           echo "servo-quickjs: \`$SERVO_QUICKJS_REF\` ($rev)" >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"
+      # `--js-engine quickjs` changes Cargo.lock, so the build is not `--locked`.
       - name: Build
-        run: ./mach build --profile "$PROFILE" --features js-quickjs
+        run: ./mach build --profile "$PROFILE" --js-engine quickjs
       - name: Smoketest
         run: xvfb-run ./mach smoketest --profile "$PROFILE"
       - name: Build mach package
diff --git a/python/servo/command_base.py b/python/servo/command_base.py
index e46e71a0b16..c9d2ddd58af 100644
--- a/python/servo/command_base.py
+++ b/python/servo/command_base.py
@@ -41,6 +41,9 @@ from python.servo.platform.build_target import SanitizerKind
 from python.servo.util import get_target_dir
 
 ASAN_LEAK_SUPPRESSION_FILE = "support/suppressed_leaks_for_asan.txt"
+JS_ENGINES = ["spidermonkey", "quickjs"]
+# The Cargo configuration of `--js-engine quickjs`, with the pinned servo-quickjs commit.
+QUICKJS_CARGO_CONFIG = "support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml"
 
 
 @dataclass
@@ -275,6 +278,7 @@ class CommandBase(object):
         self.enable_media = False
         self.enable_code_coverage = False
         self.features = []
+        self.js_engine = "spidermonkey"
 
         # Default to native build target. This will later be overriden
         # by `configure_build_target`
@@ -322,6 +326,7 @@ class CommandBase(object):
         self.config["build"].setdefault("debug-assertions", False)
         self.config["build"].setdefault("debug-mozjs", False)
         self.config["build"].setdefault("media-stack", "auto")
+        self.config["build"].setdefault("js-engine", "spidermonkey")
         self.config["build"].setdefault("ccache", "")
         self.config["build"].setdefault("rustflags", "")
         self.config["build"].setdefault("incremental", None)
@@ -503,6 +508,14 @@ class CommandBase(object):
                     choices=["gstreamer", "dummy"],
                     help="Which media stack to use",
                 ),
+                CommandArgument(
+                    "--js-engine",
+                    default=None,
+                    group="Feature Selection",
+                    choices=JS_ENGINES,
+                    help="Which JavaScript engine to build with. quickjs replaces mozjs with servo-quickjs "
+                    "and changes Cargo.lock",
+                ),
                 CommandArgument(
                     "--debug-mozjs",
                     default=False,
@@ -575,6 +588,7 @@ class CommandBase(object):
                     self.configure_build_target(kwargs)
                     self.features = kwargs.get("features", None) or []
                     self.enable_media = self.is_media_enabled(kwargs["media_stack"])
+                    self.js_engine = self.configure_js_engine(kwargs["js_engine"])
 
                 if build_configuration or binary_selection:
                     self.enable_code_coverage = kwargs.pop("coverage", False)
@@ -722,6 +736,13 @@ class CommandBase(object):
 
         return media_stack != "dummy"
 
+    def configure_js_engine(self, js_engine: Optional[str]) -> str:
+        js_engine = js_engine or self.config["build"]["js-engine"]
+        if js_engine not in JS_ENGINES:
+            print(f"Error: unknown js-engine `{js_engine}` in .servobuild, expected one of {', '.join(JS_ENGINES)}")
+            sys.exit(1)
+        return js_engine
+
     def run_cargo_build_like_command(
         self,
         command: str,
@@ -764,6 +785,10 @@ class CommandBase(object):
         elif target_override:
             args += ["--target", target_override]
 
+        # Also with `-p`, so that every command resolves the same Cargo.lock.
+        if self.js_engine == "quickjs":
+            args += ["--config", path.join(self.context.topdir, QUICKJS_CARGO_CONFIG)]
+
         features = []
 
         if use_crown:
@@ -797,6 +822,8 @@ class CommandBase(object):
                         " you are doing, consider removing `--no-default-features` from your invocation."
                     )
 
+            if self.js_engine == "quickjs":
+                features.append("js-quickjs")
             if self.config["build"]["debug-mozjs"] or debug_mozjs:
                 features.append("debugmozjs")
 
diff --git a/python/servo/pr_jobs.py b/python/servo/pr_jobs.py
index 0b3016dab2a..e4f44d365be 100644
--- a/python/servo/pr_jobs.py
+++ b/python/servo/pr_jobs.py
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ OHOS_ONLY = (
 )
 
 # Files that only the QuickJS build reads.
-QUICKJS_ONLY = (".github/workflows/quickjs.yml",)
+QUICKJS_ONLY = (".github/workflows/quickjs.yml", "support/quickjs/")
 
 # Test and expectation roots, mapped to the directory that holds their tests.
 WPT_ROOTS = {
@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@ class TestSelect(unittest.TestCase):
 
     def test_quickjs_workflow(self) -> None:
         self.assertEqual(
-            self.jobs(".github/workflows/quickjs.yml", "ports/arkweb/src/lib.rs"),
+            self.jobs(".github/workflows/quickjs.yml", "support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml", "ports/arkweb/src/lib.rs"),
             [self.LINUX, self.LINT, self.OHOS, self.QUICKJS],
         )
 
diff --git a/servobuild.example b/servobuild.example
index 7ee89eb9b49..cfa70fc132d 100644
--- a/servobuild.example
+++ b/servobuild.example
@@ -19,6 +19,11 @@ android = false
 # Enable `debug_assert!` macros in release mode
 debug-assertions = true
 
+# Set "js-engine" or use `mach build --js-engine` to pick the JavaScript engine: "spidermonkey" or
+# "quickjs", which builds on servo-quickjs (see support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml) and changes
+# Cargo.lock.
+js-engine = "spidermonkey"
+
 # Set "debug-mozjs" or use `mach build --debug-mozjs` to build a debug spidermonkey.
 debug-mozjs = false
 
diff --git a/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml b/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..a39f5ff8a7f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# The Cargo configuration of `./mach build --js-engine quickjs`. It replaces mozjs with
+# servo-quickjs, which implements the mozjs API on QuickJS.
+#
+# Bump the commit with mozjs at each sync, so that older commits keep building with the shim they
+# were tested with. The shim's version must match the mozjs version that Cargo.toml requires, or
+# Cargo leaves the patch unused.
+[patch.crates-io]
+mozjs = { git = "https://github.com/openharmony-rs/servo-quickjs", rev = "72fa2b6697a60889969397313ad23405196c5b4e" }
